        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P(A\\mid B)=\\dfrac{\\frac{1}{4}}{\\frac{1}{2}}=\\dfrac12=P(A)$, so $A$ and $B$ are independent.",
          "worked": "The four equally likely outcomes are $HH,HT,TH,TT$, and $A\\cap B=\\{TH\\}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A)&=\\frac24=\\frac12\\\\P(B)&=\\frac24=\\frac12\\\\P(A\\cap B)&=\\frac14\\\\P(A\\mid B)&=\\frac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(B)}\\\\P(A\\mid B)&=\\frac{1/4}{1/2}=\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\nSince $P(A\\mid B)=P(A)$, $A$ and $B$ are independent.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
